   FAIRFAX, VA, JUL 26-28, 2001},
Organization = {USN Off Res; Natl Sci Fdn; USAF Res Lab Human Effectiveness Directorate;
   CHI Syst; BBN Technologies},
Abstract = {In this paper a tool will be presented that simulates human perception
   and motor behavior in interaction with graphical user interfaces in the
   Microsoft Windows environment. The simulated hand and eye tool can be
   used in combination with any cognitive architecture. In order to
   validate the simulated hand and eye an experiment has been conducted in
   which human subjects showed simple, low-level interaction behavior. Eye
   movements and finger presses were measured and recorded. This allowed
   for basic validation of the simulated hand and eye. Furthermore, based
   on the collected data, an adjustment of the EMMA theory is suggested. To
   demonstrate the full usage if the tool, ACT-R has been used to model
   basic skill acquisition in instructed interaction behavior.},
