Organization = {European Neural Network Soc; Int Neural Network Soc; Japanese Neural
   Network Soc; IEEE Computat Intelligence Soc},
Abstract = {An n-class problem is decomposed into n two-class problems. Naturally,
   modular multilayer perceptions (MLPs) come into being. A single-output
   MLP is behalf of a class and trained by a two-class learning subset. A
   training subset only consists of all samples from a special class and a
   part samples from the nearest classes. If the decision boundary of a
   single-output MLP is open, its outputs are amended by a correction
   coefficient. This paper clarifies such a fact that the generalization of
   a single-output MLP is seriously affected by the sample disequilibrium
   situation. Therefore, the samples from the little class have to be
   multiplied an enlarging factor. The result of letter recognition shows
   that the above methods are effective.},
