Year = {2015},
Pages = {190-195},
Note = {International Conference on Sociology and Psychology (ICSP), Changsha,
   PEOPLES R CHINA, JAN 10-11, 2015},
Abstract = {Figure-ground phenomenon is a very important notion of gestalt theory.
   It refers to the characteristic organization of perception into a figure
   that ``stands out{''} against an undifferentiated background. Doris
   Lessing's The Golden Notebook solidified her position as a central
   figure in the English literature. In the novel, she skillfully parodies
   the myth of Oedipus and Sisyphus, as well as Joyce's Ulysses to realize
   her profound thinking and exploration in literature, language,
   psychology, mythology. According to the figure-ground theory, this paper
   will mainly focus on the readers' psychological cognitive mechanisms
   involved in comprehending literary discourse and conclude that figure
   and ground is the fundamental characteristic of literary analysis, in
   hope of providing a fresh perspective for studying literary works.},
