   through Halotherapy treatment},
Booktitle = {MENTAL HEALTH: ACTUAL VIEWS IN PSYCHOLOGY, MEDICINE AND ANTHROPOLOGY},
Year = {2016},
Pages = {70-74},
Note = {International Conference on Mental Health - Psychology, Medicine and
   Anthropology for Life Quality, Ploiesti, ROMANIA, SEP 09-11, 2016},
Abstract = {Halotherapy is a treatment method that is based on artificially
   recreating the microclimate conditions of salt mines. Simulation of the
   natural therapeutic factors of the underground environment of salt mines
   and the development of halotherapheutical chambers with artificial
   curative environment on the surface is a problem of scientific
   complexity. Subsequently a test was conducted on 20 patients with
   asthma, chronic bronchitis, allergic rhinitis and chronic obstructive
   pulmonary disease which were evaluated clinically and have also
   completed a questionnaire which assessed their own perception of how
   their disease affect their lives Some preliminary results indicate a
   increase of life quality of patients who have undergone Halotherapy.
   Comprehensive evaluation of the halotherapeutic effect and final results
   will be communicated and published later.},
