Note = {5th Regional Geoheritage Conference, Makassar, INDONESIA, SEP 23-27,
   2024},
Abstract = {This study investigates how academic institutions can contribute to
   enhancing the geopark potential of Gunung Padang in Cianjur, Indonesia.
   As a significant megalithic site in Southeast Asia, Gunung Padang
   combines geological and cultural heritage, offering valuable
   opportunities for geotourism and education. However, limited research
   and awareness hinder the full realization of these assets. This research
   focuses on perspectives within the Islamic boarding school community,
   particularly Al Kautsar Islamic Boarding School, to understand local
   perceptions of the site's potential as a tourism destination. Using
   literature reviews and key informant interviews, the study analyzes the
   role of local educational institutions in promoting environmental
   stewardship and community involvement. By integrating geopark concepts
   into educational curricula, these institutions can foster sustainable
   development, bridging cultural preservation with economic growth through
   tourism.},
