   DEVELOPMENT AND TEACHER TRAINING},
Year = {1997},
Pages = {93-95},
Note = {25th Annual Conference of the North American Association for
   Environmental Education, SAN FRANCISCO BAY AREA, CA, NOV 01-05, 1996},
Organization = {N Amer Assoc Environm Educ},
Abstract = {Teachers reported what they were experiencing, thinking and learning
   while studying in and about the out-of-doors, in an Eisenhower-funded
   program in Northeast Alabama. During this time they: bonded with each
   other and the Earth reflected about the teaching process about and with
   the environment experienced a rebirth about what is means to be human in
   community with Earth.
   These learnings were facilitated through the teachings of a Florida
   Creek Indian Medicine Maker (shaman). Participants words were recorded
   and will be used to elucidate their changing feelings, perceptions,
   roles and responsibilities and thoughts about their relationship with
   Earth and Earth species. Participants reported a rebirth and deepening
   commitment to an Earth trust and teaching about living in harmony with
   nature.},
