   Sci; Russian Acad Sci; Serbian Acad Sci \& Arts; Slovak Acad Sci Intro;
   Natl Acad Sci Ukraine; Natl Acad Sci Armenia; Sci Counc Japan; World
   Acad Sci TWAS; European Acad Sci, Arts \& Lett; Acad Fine Arts Zagreb
   Croatia; Croatian Acad Sci \& Arts; Acad Sci Moldova; Montenegrin Acad
   Sci \& Arts; Georgian Acad Sci; Acad Fine Arts \& Design Bratislava;
   Russian Acad Arts; Turkish Acad Sci; SGEM},
Abstract = {A swift acceleration of global processes nowadays, intensification of
   new tendencies in world development call for setting new priorities in
   dynamically changing world. Providing security is a fundamental priority
   of international safety. So, all efforts must be concentrated on
   achieving the following basic aims:
   - Providing national safety, keeping and strengthening sovereignty and
   territorial integrity.
   - Building favorable conditions for steady and dynamic growth, raising
   the standard of life.
   - Consolidating world peace, general security and stability.
   - Establishing good neighbourly relations.
   - Developing multilateral, mutually beneficial relations.
   - Rendering assistance in constructive dialogue and partnership in
   behalf of strengthening accord and mutual enrichment of different
   cultures and religions.
   - Popularizing cultural achievements of mankind and humanistic values.
   Literature has always been considered to be the privileged priority that
   people all over the world have created for a long period of their
   existence for intercultural communication. Literature is an art to see
   the world. Every piece of fiction is thought to be the form of indirect
   cross-cultural communication. The peculiarity of works of art are
   defined by the aims of the authors to create a figurative picture of the
   world reflecting national mentality, social, historic and cultural
   paradigm and the inner world of the people.
   A text is a form of discourse and comprehensive functional whole which
   reveals a great number of meanings within a cross-cultural system. It
   appears in unity of explicit and implicit, literal and figurative
   senses. The process of the interpretation of the text is multilevel:
   perception, cognition, understanding in the context of the national
   culture and interaction.
   The perception of literal works depends on many factors: communicative
   aims, background knowledge of both the author and the reader, specific
   character of ethnographic, historical, geographic, social phenomena. The
   cognition of realities of foreign culture in fiction gives evidence of
   national peculiarities between native and foreign cultures, requires
   knowledge of definite historical-cultural context. Otherwise, inadequate
   interpretation of phenomena of strange culture may arise.},
