   Hong Kong Inst Util Specialists},
Abstract = {More than 20\% of the world's energy is consumed on transportation. In
   the long term, vehicle design, energy and fuel technologies may
   significantly reduce the impact on environment. In the short term,
   logistics and fleet management of companies play an important role in
   sustainable urbanization. This paper proposes fleet management
   benchmarking with an objective of enhancing fuel efficiency should be
   carried out at levels of corporate and country. An analysis on how
   benchmarking study can be carried out with reference to experience
   abroad is presented. Based on a case study, it is found that an energy
   efficiency benchmarking exercise for a corporate fleet help achieve cost
   saving on fuel and enhance overall efficiency.},
