Note = {Conference on Advanced Research on Business, Management and Humanities
   (ARBUHUM), Bandung, INDONESIA, MAR 15-17, 2016},
Organization = {Malaysia Tech Scientist Assoc},
Abstract = {Taiwan has major issue related to safety. Around 80\% accident
   occurrences in Taiwan were caused by unsafe behavior. In the other hand,
   the definition of culture as ``the way we do things around here{''}
   links culture to behavior. Thus, it could be stated that poor safety
   culture contributes to the accident occurrence in Taiwan. In addition,
   it is proven that different safety perception arises among workers with
   different background. Therefore, this research aimed to investigate
   safety culture in Taiwan metal industries by emphasizing workers
   background factors. One main metal company with its five subsidiary
   companies in Taiwan were assessed using questionnaire. 839 workers were
   participated the study from total 1865 previously targeted workers. one
   way ANOVA result showed that workers background needs to be considered
   when dealing with safety culture.},
