   Portuguese-Society-of-Occupational-Safety-and-Hygiene(SHO), Guimaraes,
   PORTUGAL, MAR 23-24, 2016},
Organization = {Portuguese Soc Occupat Safety \& Hygiene; Univ Minho, Sch Engn; Univ
   Porto, Fac Engn; Univ Lisbon, Fac Human Kinet; Polytechn Univ Catalonia;
   Tech Univ Delft; Faculdade Motricidade Humana; DELTA; EXIM; ACT;
   European Agcy Safety \& Hlth Work; Lavoro},
Abstract = {The aims of the present study are to verify which work conditions and
   characteristics that Portuguese physiotherapists are exposed to, their
   relation with health and the differences between male and female. The
   INSAT (Work and Health Survey) was used. Working conditions related to
   contact with the public and to physical constraints, as well as
   emotional demands, do affect physiotherapists. There are differences
   between men and women regarding the exposure and discomfort with the
   different work constraints. Physiotherapists perceive that their health
   is affected by their work and this perception is positively associated
   with work conditions and characteristics to which the physiotherapists
   are exposed. The most common health problems reported are back pain and
   musculoskeletal disorders. These problems are also the ones that most
   physiotherapists relate to the work.},
