Abstract = {The concept of quality of life is based on the recognition that growth
   brings prosperity increase life satisfaction. An important finding is
   that it can grow, it can only get better or get worse. Aristotle in
   Nicomachean Ethic quality of life divided into eudaimonic and
   hedonistic. In the environmental context, the perception of quality
   comes to the fore in connection with the finding of a low valuation of
   socio-economic aspects of sustainable development, as one of the four
   pillars of sustainability. Sustainable development has been redefined as
   a holistic concept of quality of life. In terms of quality of life
   ecology in the paper regarded as environmental ethics, one of the
   indicators or one of the domains. The focus is on basic aspects of the
   diffusion of ecological ethics and quality of life.},
