Note = {22nd Congress of the International Ergonomics Association-IEA, SOUTH
   KOREA, AUG 25-29, 2024},
Abstract = {There is no doubt that reduplication plays an important role in the
   grammar of various countries, such as being more vivid or more cute.
   Most of the current studies put forward their roles and viewpoints from
   a qualitative perspective. This study explores the influence of
   reduplicated words and the pressure scenes used in them on user
   experience in speech interaction from the perspective of behavioural
   experiments. The final results show that in daily low-pressure scenes,
   the use of positive overlapping words has a better user experience. In
   high-pressure scenes, even if no overlapping words are used, the use of
   negative overlapping words should be avoided as much as possible. At the
   end of the paper, it also discusses the different perceptions of users
   with different personality traits.},
