Abstract = {When a fire breaks throughout the exterior of a fire compartment, there
   is the possibility of vertical spread on the facade of the building,
   threatening the apartments of the upper floors. The main regulation in
   Romania (SC007-2013) states a number of technical and constructive
   requirements in order to limit the vertical spread of fire to the
   buildings which are thermal insulated with polystyrene. The aim of this
   research paper is to present the behavior of the proposed systems and
   solutions in case of fire and to optimize the width of a non-combustible
   barrier system to achieve the desired effect. There are also presented
   three laboratory tests for different design parameters and are being
   analyzed the results from fire exposure according to ISO 834
   time-temperature curve. (C) 2017 Published by Elsevier Ltd.},
