   Pedroso Construc S A; Moniz Maia Serra \& Fortunato, Empreiteiros S A;
   MOTA \& COMPANHIA S A; ENGIL, Soc Construc Civil S A},
Abstract = {Relying on extensive experience, as well as the results of recent
   research, the authors have reached a number of conclusions concerning
   the prospects for collaboration in the development of practical
   applications of expert systems, virtual reality, and other computer
   based applications. These applications are intended to be used by
   workers and professionals for construction accident prevention. This
   paper discusses the authors' opinion of potential approaches for future
   international collaboration towards the prevention of construction
   accidents. Their perceptions of the need, practicability, and
   desirability of international collaboration are reported. Two areas of
   concern are identified: (1) the need for a `'code of ethics'' to protect
   the interests of the participating parties; and (2) the establishment
   and maintenance of World Wide Web (WWW) sites including intranets
   (private networks on the internet).},
